  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M.K.Antony vs Bjp Vanijya Vyavasaya Cell on 1 April, 2014 Author: A.M.Shaffique Bench: A.M.Shaffique In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable The Chief Justice Mr.Ashok Bhushan & The Honourable Mr.Justice A.M.Shaffique Thursday, The 14Th Day Of January 2016/24Th Pousha, 1937 WP(C).No. 35345 of 2014 (P) ---------------------------- Petitioner(S): -------------------------- 1. M.K.Antony,S/O.Kuriappan, Aged 60 Years, Room No.52, Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Residing At Muthipeedika House, Kuriyachira. 2. N.A. Jaleel, S/O.Aboobacker, Room No.54, (Aged 54 Years), Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Residing At Njaveliparambil House, Ollukara, Thrissur District. 3. T.T. Francis, Room No.21, Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Residing At Thattil Umbavoo (H), Aranattukara. 4 . P.A. Hassan, Room No.35, Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Residing At Panikkaveettil Valiyaparambil (H), Post Koorkencherry, Thrissur. 5. Godfrey, Room No.50, Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Residing At Arrangasserry House, Industrial Estate Road, P.O. Ollur, Thrissur District. M.K.Antony vs Bjp Vanijya Vyavasaya Cell on 1 April, 2014 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/195909393/ 1 6. P.K. Chandran, Room 20, Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Residing At Paraparambil House, Anchery Post, Ollur, Thrissur District. 7. T.P.Jose, Room No.46, Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Residing At Thattilumbavoo House, P.O. Pullazhi, Olarikkara, Thrissur District. 8. K.G. Santhosh, Room No.47, Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Kuriyedath House, Peramangalam P.O., Thrissur District. WP(C).No. 35345 of 2014 (P) 9. Mary Varghese, W/O.A.L. Varghese, Room No.49, Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Arrangasserry House, P.O. Pookunnam, Thrissur. 10. A.S. Vijayalakshmy,Room No.51, Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Residing At Kadavi House, P.O. Koorkanchery. 11. Jose T.J., Room 66, Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Residing At Thattil Umbavu House, Aranattukara, Thrissur. 12. V.M. Abbas, Room 48, Shakthanthampuran Fish Market, Thrissur, Residing At Valiyakath House, Kurumpilavu, Thrissur District. By Adv. Sri.M.P.Ashok Kumar. Respondent(S): ---------------------------- 1. Bjp Vanijya Vyavasaya Cell, Represented By Its Secretary, A.S. Nazeer, Stall No.93, Sakthanthampuran Non-Vegetarian Market, Thrissur - 680 001. 2. The Circle Inspector Of Police, Thrissur East Police Station, Thrissur District - 680 003. 3. The Sub Inspector Of Police, M.K.Antony vs Bjp Vanijya Vyavasaya Cell on 1 April, 2014 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/195909393/ 2 Thrissur Town East Police Station, Thrissur District - 680 003. 4. The Thrissur Municipal Corporation, Thrissur - 680 001, Represented By Its Secretary. R1 By Sri.Renjith Thampan, Senior Advocate. Adv. Smt.P.R.Reena. R2 & R3 By Sr. Govt. Pleader Sri.C.R. Syamkumar. R4 By Advs. Sri.K.P.Vijayan, Sri.V.N.Haridas . THIS WRIT PETITION (CIVIL) HAVING BEEN FINALLY HEARD ON 14-01-2016, THE COURT ON THE SAME DAY DELIVERED THE FOLLOWING: rs. WP(C).No. 35345 of 2014 (P) APPENDIX PETITIONER'S EXHIBITS:- EXT.P-1: PHOTOCOPY OF THE LICENSE ISSUED BY THE FOOD SAFETY AND STANDARDS AUTHORITY OF INDIA UNDER THE FOOD SAFETY AND STANDARDS ACT 2006 DATED 01.04.2014.",
    "facts": "It is stated that petitioners are licensed whole sale raw fish merchants doing business in the Sakthanthampuram public market maintained by the Municipal Corporation of Trichur. Certain issues had arisen between retailers, who, according to the petitioners, also started wholesale business. This has resulted in law and order situation. Though the petitioners approached the police seeking necessary protection, no action has been taken in the matter and hence the petitioners have approached this Court. 2. Counter affidavit has been filed by the 4th respondent inter alia stating that separate areas and timings are alloted to both the groups regarding conduct of trade in the market. Meetings were convened including whole sale traders and the issues had virtually been settled. It is also stated that the Corporation is taking all earnest efforts to resolve the dispute between the rival traders. 3. Counter affidavit has been filed by the 1st respondent stating that there are more than 33 licensees conducting fish vending in the respective stalls, who had obtained necessary licence from the Municipality as well as from other competent authorities. According to them, the intention in filing the writ petition is to prevent the respondents and their men from carrying on the fish vending activities as permitted under valid licence.",
    "arguments": "4. Facts being so, learned counsel for the petitioners submits that during the pendency of the writ petition, there was no untoward incident.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. Facts being so, learned counsel for the petitioners submits that during the pendency of the writ petition, there was no untoward incident.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
